e king earlier  when she interviewed you that you said  that justice for you would mean that she  spends uh her life behind bars  does that seem like a real possibility  now  i mean just just the mere thought of  that i just  i mean it's so mind-boggling it still  hasn't dawned on me that justice has  finally been served it's  you know it's been such a long hard  journey to get here  so yesterday's decision i think will  take um  a little while to to sink in  but um  the thought of guillain spending the  rest of her life behind bars  you know you must understand she  she destroyed  so many hundreds if not thousands  of other women young women and children  you know so  i'm i'm pleased that she will never  she'll never be out again ever to hurt  anybody else and for that i feel very  pleased  and that's when you it really was  because of those four women who  testified a big chunk of this you said  in 2017  you sued epstein and maxwell settle with  them for an undisclosed amount of money  you have said in the past that you wish  that you had had your day in court  how do you feel now  well i sort of did have my day in court  you know these these brave women gave me  my day in court you know and that's why  it was so important for for me to be  there in new york during the trial  and  you know i  i got that moment with elaine  um on closing arguments i sat um  a verb behind  elaine's family and  i had that eye connection with gilean  and  i'll never forget when she forced me  into a room to be raped by jeffrey and  the way she smiled  and  now  guillen will remember  that look when i sat behind her family  for the rest of her life and it's just a  wonderful feeling  was it hard for you to be in court  i was terrified you know i mean you know  i think of myself as brave and strong  and i  i remember the the morning before um  i i was finally  finally uh able to get into the main  courtroom and i just i was terrified but  then  you know when i sat there  and saw her for what she really is  she looked pathetic  absolutely pathetic and it was worth  every single dollar  i spent being in new york  and it will be a moment i will treasure  for the rest of my life it was worth  every  moment  it sounds like a very powerful moment  for you  um in your mind do you feel she's worse  than epstein  yes i do  you're so sorry yes i do  um  women are supposed to look after each  other  human beings are supposed to look after  each other  and  because she was a woman she normalized  abuse  she participated  she tortured  me and and  and others and  she's worse than jeffrey she broke the  sisterhood  she broke that bond  she was supposed to be a protector and  nurturer  and she failed us  and she'll have to live with that for  the rest of her life  sarah i can only imagine how hard this  is for you and in the past you've talked  about victim shaming and there was a lot  of victim shaming for years uh when  talking about jeffrey epstein and glenn  maxwell  do you feel that talking about this  today hearing this verdict writing your  book  um  do you feel like it's part of your  healing process  i am a completely different woman from  when i started writing the book to the  woman i am now  i  the book for me  was not only about my personal growth it  was about me taking responsibilities for  for  some of the mistakes i've made and  i have been called every single name  under the sun i mean you name it i've  been called it and you know what it's  it's actually made me unbreakable and  that was a reason why i wrote the book  because yes i've made so many mistakes  i'm a human being who doesn't  um i don't go out harming anybody the  only person i harmed was myself  but it doesn't mean  that i i'm not  i'm not a victim of rape or sex  trafficking  so  you know the victim shaming needs to  stop  and i hope that my my book has in some  way paved the way  for other victims to go you know what  it doesn't matter if i did this or that  i'm still a victim  i i still deserve a voice i still  deserve to be heard  and and my book  you know i just want if i can do  anything  is to just say  don't be silence silence no more  you know we are in a new era  you know this  this case with gillane is absolutely  groundback-breaking  this is history-making  and i think  you know this is an example that  you know the powerful the wealthy  you can't behave like this  you will eventually be stopped  and i hope people think  really long and hard  next time they want to hurt another  human being  sarah so many important messages and  what you're talking about this morning  thank you so much for sharing your story  we appreciate you being here  thank you very much thank you
 

